      "reason": "data_card.md is NO-GO on one mechanized leakage row: 615 row-content hashes straddle the partitions (5.12% of development rows, 5.32% of sealed rows have a byte-identical training twin). Accepted, not fixed, for three reasons on the record in program.md: (1) the cause is the dataset's coarse rating structure, not this study's preparation - 6.1% of the whole table sits in a duplicate-content group, and tables/duplicate_exposure.tsv shows the v1 study this port reproduces carried the same 5.22% in its own validation partition, unmeasured; (2) both available fixes (dedupe in prepare.py, or a content-hash group split) change which rows are trained on, which destroys the train-partition identity with v1 that predictions P1, P2 and P4 are registered against, and repairs nothing about the v1 number being reproduced; (3) policy_id, the only identifier of an individual policy, is dropped and crosses nothing - what the check reports is feature resolution, and for a rating model the modelling unit is the cell, not the policy. The risk is carried with a number attached: train.py prints twin_free_rows, twin_free_auc and twin_free_gap on every run, so every rung reports its AUC on the evaluation rows with no training twin, and findings scope every generalisation sentence by that gap. data_card.md is left saying NO-GO - the auditor's verdict is not edited to unlock a gate.",
